WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:23.180
999 DAYS:
On February 25, 2020, Bob Chapek was promoted

00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:26.000
to being CEO of Walt Disney.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:28.320
Disney was doing better than ever before.

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:33.200
They had just released Frozen 2 a few months
ago and it was breaking box office records

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:34.780
left and right.

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:39.370
Meanwhile, Disney Plus had just been launched
3 months ago and it was growing faster than

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:41.610
even Disney could imagine.

00:00:41.610 --> 00:00:46.530
People were watching movies more than ever,
traveling more than ever, and Covid was just

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:48.899
something that you read about on the news.

00:00:48.899 --> 00:00:54.840
But, just 17 days after his promotion, the
United States would enter a national lockdown

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:59.690
and enter one of the most unprecedented times
in history.

00:00:59.690 --> 00:01:05.920
Overnight, all Disney Parks shutdown, no one
was watching Disney movies in theaters, and

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:08.490
Disney couldn’t even produce their films
in person.

00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:12.750
Disney had entered one of the worst crises
in its history and the man at the helm had

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:15.939
been there for a whopping 17 days.

00:01:15.939 --> 00:01:20.229
Over the next two years, Disney would experience
some of their lowest lows and some of their

00:01:20.229 --> 00:01:22.000
highest highs.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:26.799
Disney Plus would rocket to over 100 million
subscribers putting Netflix to shame.

00:01:26.799 --> 00:01:31.799
But at the same time, their multi hundred
million dollar parks would be completely deserted

00:01:31.799 --> 00:01:33.870
like some wasteland.

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:39.010
Despite the glorious highs and terrible lows,
it seemed like Disney was overall on the right

00:01:39.010 --> 00:01:40.010
track.

00:01:40.010 --> 00:01:44.920
By mid 2021, Disney stock was setting new
all time highs, crossing over $200 billion

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:46.250
in market cap.

00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:48.600
But all of this would change in 2022.

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:53.649
The first signs of a recession could be seen
over the horizon and as people pulled back

00:01:53.649 --> 00:01:57.340
on spending, Disney would be hit harder than
the pandemic.

00:01:57.340 --> 00:02:04.189
Day after day, Disney would put in new 52
week low, new 52 week low, new 52 week low.

00:02:04.189 --> 00:02:07.070
In fact, they would return to their pandemic
lows.

00:02:07.070 --> 00:02:11.980
And it turned out that Disney plus wasn’t
nearly as successful as the media had led

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:13.560
us to believe.

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:18.069
Subscriber numbers were plummeting, the platform
was losing billions, and there were even signs

00:02:18.069 --> 00:02:20.870
that there may have been some accounting fraud.

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:26.610
Obviously, shareholders were furious and at
the end of 999 days, it was decided that Bob

00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:29.310
Chapek had done more harm than good.

00:02:29.310 --> 00:02:34.560
And in November of 2022, Bob Chapek would
be fired from being Disney’s CEO.

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:39.400
To rub salt in the wound, his replacement
would be his predecessor Bob Iger, something

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:42.340
that Disney fans would celebrate.

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:51.159
So, here’s Bob Chapek’s tumultuous 999
days at the top and why he was really fired

00:02:51.159 --> 00:02:52.920
from the top job.

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:58.510
DISNEY+ FRAUD (ALLEGEDLY):
Jumping straight into it, Disney allegedly

00:02:58.510 --> 00:03:04.069
discovered that Bob Chapek was cooking the
books to hide the massive losses of Disney+.

00:03:04.069 --> 00:03:06.900
It’s not surprising why he would do this.

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:11.560
He had just taken over as CEO during one of
the worst periods of the company’s history.

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:15.670
And if he wanted to stick around and impress
shareholders, he had to put up impressive

00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:16.670
numbers.

00:03:16.670 --> 00:03:21.750
But, that was nearly impossible when half
of your business is shut down and the other

00:03:21.750 --> 00:03:25.720
half is charging super low subscription fees
just to get people in the door.

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:31.099
So, Chapek allegedly turned to the good old
fudge the numbers and hope no one notices.

00:03:31.099 --> 00:03:34.090
Honestly, it was quite clever what he did.

00:03:34.090 --> 00:03:37.330
He didn’t just pull numbers out of thin
air or make up numbers.

00:03:37.330 --> 00:03:41.659
Instead, he would simply rearrange some expenses
to make certain parts of the business look

00:03:41.659 --> 00:03:43.460
better than they really were.

00:03:43.460 --> 00:03:48.870
The best example of this was with two TV series
called The Mysterious Benedict Society and

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:50.349
Doogie Kamealoha MD.

00:03:50.349 --> 00:03:55.730
The production cost of these series is not
known, but it was likely in the tens of millions.

00:03:55.730 --> 00:04:00.680
If we call it $50 million each, we have a
total production cost of about $100 million,

00:04:00.680 --> 00:04:03.079
and there’s also marketing on top of that,
so quite a sizable expense.

00:04:03.079 --> 00:04:07.959
But, Chapek allegedly found a clever way to
offload this cost from Disney+.

00:04:07.959 --> 00:04:13.510
You see, he would air these shows on the Disney
Channel slightly before airing them on Disney+.

00:04:13.510 --> 00:04:17.530
This way he could write off the marketing
and production expenses of the show as a Disney

00:04:17.530 --> 00:04:20.790
channel expense as opposed to a Disney+ expense.

00:04:20.790 --> 00:04:25.970
So, instead of costing $50 million each, it
appeared that they only cost $20 or $30 million.

00:04:25.970 --> 00:04:26.970
This might not sound like a big deal.

00:04:26.970 --> 00:04:29.900
I mean as far as we know, he was marking down
the right numbers.

00:04:29.900 --> 00:04:34.060
He was just clevely spreading the cost across
Disney’s various media sectors.

00:04:34.060 --> 00:04:38.360
But, while clever, this is also extremely
misleading.

00:04:38.360 --> 00:04:42.690
Investors are suddenly led to believe that
these shows achieved an extraordinary ROI

00:04:42.690 --> 00:04:44.660
in terms of cost vs viewership leading them
to approve not so great choices.

00:04:44.660 --> 00:04:49.280
For example, this tactic made it seem like
launching movies on Disney+ was more worth

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:50.830
it than it really was.

00:04:50.830 --> 00:04:56.330
If a $10 million show was able to garner this
much watch time, imagine what a $150 million

00:04:56.330 --> 00:04:57.940
flagship movie could bring in.

00:04:57.940 --> 00:05:00.380
The truth is not much.

00:05:00.380 --> 00:05:03.710
While streaming plaforms are a great way to
earn recurring revenue on movies that have

00:05:03.710 --> 00:05:08.440
already had their run in theaters, it’s
a terrible way to monetize new releases.

00:05:08.440 --> 00:05:10.910
But, due to potential funny business, the
board and investors weren’t exactly aware

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:15.669
of this and they would allow for movies like
Soul, Disenchanted, and Hocus Pocus 2 to directly

00:05:15.669 --> 00:05:17.030
launch on Disney+.

00:05:17.030 --> 00:05:22.020
And given that Chapek couldn’t do any slight
of hand with these big name films, it didn’t

00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:25.009
take long for investors to realize the truth
about Disney+.

00:05:25.009 --> 00:05:30.180
And, let’s just say Disney is now taking
the exact opposite approach when it comes

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:32.350
to bringing movies to Disney+.

00:05:32.350 --> 00:05:37.419
With Avatar 2, for example, Disney hasn’t
even provided a release Disney+ release timeframe.

00:05:37.419 --> 00:05:43.080
It’s rumored though that it wont come out
till July or 7 months after the initial release.

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:47.441
If Chapek didn’t allegedly play with the
numbers, maybe executives could have come

00:05:47.441 --> 00:05:52.410
to this conclusion way quicker like Universal
Studios did with James Bond No Time To Die,

00:05:52.410 --> 00:05:58.040
but instead they ended up releasing big budget
films on Disney+ and losing a bunch of money.

00:05:58.040 --> 00:06:03.690
Not only is Chapek’s supposed actions misleading,
but in court, it could be argued to be securities

00:06:03.690 --> 00:06:04.690
fraud.

00:06:04.690 --> 00:06:09.780
After all, misleading investors is against
SEC rules and regulation, but that’s not

00:06:09.780 --> 00:06:14.970
where the story ends as Disney+ wasn’t the
only place where some funny business may have

00:06:14.970 --> 00:06:16.220
occurred either.

00:06:16.220 --> 00:06:21.530
DISNEY PARK FRAUD (ALLEGEDLY):
According to whistleblower Sandy Kuba, Disney

00:06:21.530 --> 00:06:26.340
was also cooking the books with their Disney
Parks for years well before Chapek tookover

00:06:26.340 --> 00:06:27.340
as CEO.

00:06:27.340 --> 00:06:32.580
But, that doesn’t mean that Chapek is in
the clear because guess what Chapek’s job

00:06:32.580 --> 00:06:34.550
was before he became CEO?

00:06:34.550 --> 00:06:40.111
Well, he was the chairman of Disney Parks
and Resorts since 2015, so it doesn’t seem

00:06:40.111 --> 00:06:43.310
like the Disney+ thing was his first offense.

00:06:43.310 --> 00:06:48.120
According to Sandy Kuba, Disney was religiously
employing accounting tricks to overstate park

00:06:48.120 --> 00:06:49.120
revenues.

00:06:49.120 --> 00:06:52.199
Here are some of the tricks that Disney allegedly
leveraged.

00:06:52.199 --> 00:06:56.000
You know how sometimes you can get gift cards
for discounted prices?

00:06:56.000 --> 00:07:01.360
For example, you might be able to get a $500
gift card for $395 or something.

00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:05.940
Well, Disney regularly sells gift cards for
discounts, but instead recording the amount

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:10.400
that customers actually paid for the gift
card, Disney would allegedly just record the

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:12.570
face value of the giftcard.

00:07:12.570 --> 00:07:17.300
And when you’re talking about giftcards
that are regularly discounted by 20%, you’re

00:07:17.300 --> 00:07:20.940
constantly overstating you’re giftcard revenue
by 20%.

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:24.830
This wasn’t the only gift card trick Disney
had up their sleeve either.

00:07:24.830 --> 00:07:29.130
Whenever they gave out free gift cards to
angry customers, well that was apparently

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:31.250
counted as earned revenue as well.

00:07:31.250 --> 00:07:35.860
Also, Disney would supposedly count the revenue
of each gift card twice, once when it was

00:07:35.860 --> 00:07:38.460
purchased and once when it was used.

00:07:38.460 --> 00:07:42.220
It seems like some of these tricks didn’t
just apply to gift cards either.

00:07:42.220 --> 00:07:46.560
It appears that Disney was regularly was regularly
marking down all sorts of complimentary items

00:07:46.560 --> 00:07:47.930
as earned revenue.

00:07:47.930 --> 00:07:52.210
For example, let’s say you booked a hotel
with Disney and received a complimentary round

00:07:52.210 --> 00:07:54.970
of golf that’s valued at a $100.

00:07:54.970 --> 00:07:59.320
Disney would apparently mark this down as
earned revenue even though you didn’t pay

00:07:59.320 --> 00:08:00.320
anything for it.

00:08:00.320 --> 00:08:04.470
Also, it’s not like someone was manually
making these changes on the fly.

00:08:04.470 --> 00:08:09.039
These tricks were apparently baked into the
software itself making it easy to systematically

00:08:09.039 --> 00:08:14.060
overstate revenue by billions of dollars and
nearly impossible to detect without being

00:08:14.060 --> 00:08:15.060
an insider.

00:08:15.060 --> 00:08:18.730
Sandy would of course try to sort out these
issues internally at first.

00:08:18.730 --> 00:08:23.680
She tried contacting senior executives and
the auditing team, but they obviously didn’t

00:08:23.680 --> 00:08:25.789
do anything other than threaten her.

00:08:25.789 --> 00:08:30.780
They informed her that if she reported her
concerns about the company’s practices elsewhere,

00:08:30.780 --> 00:08:33.709
Disney would consider it retaliation against
the company.

00:08:33.709 --> 00:08:38.500
Honestly, it would’ve been in Sandy’s
best interest to just keep quiet, but she

00:08:38.500 --> 00:08:41.020
would decide to do the brave thing and report
it to the SEC.

00:08:41.020 --> 00:08:45.450
I don’t think you’d be surprised to hear
that she would be fired shortly after the

00:08:45.450 --> 00:08:46.850
SEC filing was made.

00:08:46.850 --> 00:08:51.561
It’s not clear what exactly the SEC has
been doing with this case since then, but

00:08:51.561 --> 00:08:54.149
it’s definitely not anything notable.

00:08:54.149 --> 00:08:59.670
So, for all we know, Disney could still be
leveraging such tactics to this day.

00:08:59.670 --> 00:09:04.310
Also, according to Sandy, the worst of it
was during the 2008 financial crisis when

00:09:04.310 --> 00:09:08.690
Disney may have overstated their revenues
by as much as $6 billion.

00:09:08.690 --> 00:09:14.399
For perspective, Disney’s total park revenue
in 2009 was $10.6 billion which means that

00:09:14.399 --> 00:09:17.399
as much as 60% of this revenue may have been
fraudulent.

00:09:17.399 --> 00:09:24.029
With that being said, we just crossed an even
worse period for Disney parks in 2020 and

00:09:24.029 --> 00:09:29.280
2021, so who knows how much trickery may have
been happening behind the scenes.

00:09:29.280 --> 00:09:35.140
IT ALL FALLS DOWN:
As you can see, fudging numbers with Disney+

00:09:35.140 --> 00:09:39.620
may have just been the latest in a history
of bending the rules for Bob Chapek, but it

00:09:39.620 --> 00:09:42.350
was the first time that he faced any real
consequences.

00:09:42.350 --> 00:09:48.079
The SEC went ahead and fined Disney for I’m
just kidding, did you really think the SEC

00:09:48.079 --> 00:09:49.529
would do anything?

00:09:49.529 --> 00:09:53.360
Best case scenario, they might fine Disney
for $100 million or something.

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:56.990
The real consequences for Chapek were dealt
by the board and shareholders.

00:09:56.990 --> 00:10:01.250
I don’t think the board cared too much about
the fudging of the numbers other than the

00:10:01.250 --> 00:10:07.050
fact that that makes them look bad, but something
that they do care about is the bottom line.

00:10:07.050 --> 00:10:10.089
And Chapek wasn’t able to deliver on the
bottomline.

00:10:10.089 --> 00:10:14.850
In fact, he not only didn’t deliver, but
he put up some atrocious numbers which may

00:10:14.850 --> 00:10:16.640
have been fudged to begin with.

00:10:16.640 --> 00:10:21.459
So, in reality, these numbers are probably
worse than reported, but here’s what the

00:10:21.459 --> 00:10:23.230
reported numbers suggest.

00:10:23.230 --> 00:10:29.709
Right before, Chapek got fired, Disney+ reported
a loss of $1.5 billion in a single quarter.

00:10:29.709 --> 00:10:35.481
To simply make up for Disney’s current burn
rate, Disney needs 62.5 million people to

00:10:35.481 --> 00:10:39.769
join Disney+ and not watch anything at all
forever.

00:10:39.769 --> 00:10:45.639
This may have sounded reasonable 2 years ago
when everyone was joining due to the pandemic,

00:10:45.639 --> 00:10:48.010
but now, the exact opposite is happening.

00:10:48.010 --> 00:10:53.150
In the most recent quarter, Disney+ reported
a subscriber loss of 2.4 million.

00:10:53.150 --> 00:10:57.110
Last year, people were calling Netflix dead
for losing subscribers for the first time

00:10:57.110 --> 00:11:00.899
in 10 years, and even that was only 500,000.

00:11:00.899 --> 00:11:06.089
Disney+ over here is losing nearly 5 times
that amount after just being out for a mere

00:11:06.089 --> 00:11:07.089
3 years.

00:11:07.089 --> 00:11:11.720
Yeah, I don’t think it was very difficult
for the board to give Chapek the axe.

00:11:11.720 --> 00:11:16.880
It just so happened to be exactly 999 days
after Chapek took over.

00:11:16.880 --> 00:11:22.710
For Chapek, this was probably quite humiliating
and terrible for his reputation, but in terms

00:11:22.710 --> 00:11:25.370
of compensation, it worked out quite well.

00:11:25.370 --> 00:11:29.850
He was handed out a generous $20 million despite
driving Disney stock back to pandemic lows,

00:11:29.850 --> 00:11:34.740
making Disney+ a money pit, and potentially
misleading investors for years.

00:11:34.740 --> 00:11:40.010
In the meantime, Disney is looking to their
former CEO Bob Iger to work his magic once

00:11:40.010 --> 00:11:41.010
again.

00:11:41.010 --> 00:11:45.430
Iger was the one behind all the acquisitions
that Disney is known for today including Pixar,

00:11:45.430 --> 00:11:48.589
Marvel, Lucasfilm, and 21st Century Fox.

00:11:48.589 --> 00:11:54.110
So, Disney is hoping that Iger can pull off
a miracle with Disney+ as well, but only time

00:11:54.110 --> 00:11:55.110
will till.

00:11:55.110 --> 00:12:01.300
But, that’s the dark truth about Bob Chapek
and why he was really fired after just 999

00:12:01.300 --> 00:12:02.300
as CEO.

